Rust API
========

Rustdoc is generated with
``cargo doc --no-deps --no-default-features`` for the selected Rust output.
The generated crate exposes primitive functions through the public ``profile``
module. This reference renders a profile-neutral union of the generated Rust
primitive APIs, so no concrete machine-profile Cargo feature is selected and
each primitive appears once. Concrete profile availability and implementation
state belong to the specialization reference.

Normal crate builds still select exactly one machine profile through Cargo
features. Rust target-feature auto-selection is not implemented yet, so
selecting a non-default machine profile remains explicit.

``tsl_core`` and ``tsl_algorithm`` are the current public vector and algorithm
substrates used by those primitive functions. Generated test helpers and the
physical ``tsl_<profile>`` module names are implementation details and are
hidden from the API index.

`Open the Rust API reference <rust/index.html>`_
